# Reference Point — Subsection Head (`.overview-sub-head`)

When the user says **"reference point"** for a subsection label/head (e.g. "About the project", "Gaps that are still uncovered"), match `.overview-sub-head` in `#overview`.

## Structure

```html
<div class="overview-sub-head stack-16">
  <p class="eyebrow soft">Section label</p>
  <h3 class="title">Headline with <em>optional emphasis</em></h3>
</div>
```

Place inside a block wrapper (`.about-block`, `.gaps-block`, etc.) above its content grid.

## Visual spec

| Layer | Class | Treatment |
|-------|-------|-----------|
| Wrapper | `.overview-sub-head.stack-16` | column flex, `gap: 1rem` |
| Label | `.eyebrow.soft` | `var(--label-size)` (0.875rem), weight 500, `0.2em` tracking, uppercase, `var(--label-soft)` (#9ca3af) |
| Headline | `h3.title` | `var(--serif)`, `var(--title-sm)`, weight 400, `var(--ink-deep)`, `max-width: 40rem` |

See also **Subsection Title** reference in `reference-point-sub-title.mdc` for `h3.title` alone.
| Emphasis | `.title em` | italic serif |

## vs other eyebrows

| Context | Class | Color |
|---------|-------|-------|
| Main section | `.eyebrow` | brown `var(--label)` |
| Subsection (this reference) | `.eyebrow.soft` | grey `var(--label-soft)` |
| Role card | `.role-card .eyebrow` | `#6b7280`, 0.75rem |

## Do not

- Use `.display` for subsection headlines — reserve for main section heads.
- Use `.role-card` for this pattern — card is a separate reference point.
- Apply brown `.eyebrow` on subsections — always `.eyebrow.soft`.
